  "study_note": "Targeted follow-up on Qwen3.5 9B, Ministral 3B, Gemini Flash-Lite, and Sonnet. Three conditions share a $2 per-run model-spend allowance, a $24 study ceiling, 30 minutes, 80 responses and 120 executions; no cumulative token cap. A conservative pre-request cost bound and reservations for unknown charges may stop a run below $2 of reported charges. Hybrid agents must discover relevant guides before execution, read each skill guide before invocation, prefer supported skill operations, and retain Python for unsupported steps and recovery. Scientific scores are unchanged; actual skill adoption is reported separately. Same cached task and reviewed catalog as v4. This changes prompting and budgets together, so it cannot isolate either effect and is not pooled with v4. One attempt per condition is exploratory. Astra remains excluded for benchmark-development involvement.",
